Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-21-2001||07:10 PM||||Can anyone tell me the timing specs for and 85 2m6 Se?  My emissions label is gone.  I checked the haynes manual and they say check the label (kinda like chasing my a$$ here)  Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||06-21-2001||07:32 PM||||Since we are on the subject.....<P>Could those of you with cameras get a good picture of each VECI label?<P>I need clear pictures from the 84-86 4 cyl and the V6. I'll grab one of my 87. I want to put one of each into a cave article. (Need them as GIF, BMP or TIFF. Not JPEG(JPG). it fuzzes the text to much.)<P>This would help not only Leadfoot but everyone that's replaced the deck lid as well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-21-2001||07:53 PM||||The timing for a V-6 is 10 degrees before top dead center. When viewing the timing gauge the large indent "V" near the top is 0.<BR>Each point is 2 degrees. The gauge reads 0 to 14 degrees.<BR>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-21-2001||08:37 PM||||you need to hook up a scan tool and put ecm in field service mode.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-21-2001||09:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PBJ:<BR><B>you need to hook up a scan tool and put ecm in field service mode.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Or just short out pins A and B on the ALDL connector and that will put it in by-pass/ open loop mode / Field service mode also.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||06-22-2001||01:47 PM||||That is another question.  On my old 2.5L I would short the A/B pins and then start the car, but according to my brother, who owns a 91 firebird, that is a no no.  So do I short the pins and then start the car or start the car and then short the pins? <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> Or just short out pins A and B on the ALDL connector and that will put it in by-pass/ open loop mode / Field service mode also.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steven||06-22-2001||02:47 PM||||Ground the ALDL conn first, then put key in ign., and start. You don't want there to be any kind of voltage spike getting back to the ECM. ||||reg||1
